The rotating 3D heart for Scene 9 Peace in Practice is built and verified.

The flat image and card-spin CSS transform are replaced with a real three dimensional sculpted heart mesh rendered on a 780 by 726 backing store canvas. The heart geometry derives from the parametric heart curve, puffed into over 1000 quads with Lambert diffuse, Blinn specular highlight, Fresnel rim lighting, a contact shadow beneath, and 12 orbiting 3D glints.

### What now works
1. [peace-in-practice.js](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-peace-in-practice/public/color-polish/scenes/peace-in-practice.js) builds the 3D heart mesh, projects it with perspective camera ($F = 3.2$), sorts visible quads by depth, and shades each quad across the shipped heart palette with no per-frame array allocations.
2. [peace-in-practice.css](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-peace-in-practice/public/color-polish/scenes/peace-in-practice.css) sizes `#tv .scene[data-scene="9"] #heart-host canvas` and stops animations under `#tv.still`.
3. [peace-in-practice.spec.ts](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-peace-in-practice/tests/color-polish-scenes/peace-in-practice.spec.ts) verifies the canvas exists with `role="img"`, confirms canvas frame changes between 2000 ms and 4000 ms, verifies three distinct luminance bands (shadow, base, highlight), and checks canvas presence in still mode.
4. [peace-in-practice.md](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-peace-in-practice/docs/runs/2026-09-11-tv-scenes/lanes/peace-in-practice.md) records the Round r4 result.

